_uuid":"7a7ae71e-96a2-4eff-8d5c-dd88c5b817aa","position":{"commit_sha":"c7be72cb81689d2975003f017bc3a9c11854a082","position":"1786501422002651001-7a7ae71e-96a2-4eff-8d5c-dd88c5b817aa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation note — test placement deviates from the recorded file_impact.\n\nThe three queue-bound tests (per-type open count, pre-enqueue CLAIM skip, corrupt-newest fallback) landed in tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py, not tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py as file_impact declared. test_enrich_queue.py is the cohesive home for llm/overlap/queue.py — it already owns the enqueue/soak/claim/lease/reduce suite and the fixtures these tests need. test_enrich_drain.py covers the drain-gate wiring and is unchanged; it is still run as a regression (passes).\n\nThe AC4 filename/body-timestamp coupling test landed in tests/unit/test_store.py as declared, next to the canonical-bytes tests, asserting on the real stage_and_commit output rather than re-deriving the name via event_filename.\n\nRED verified: against the pre-change queue.py the two bound tests fail — reduce opened 90 queue files (now <= 3) and claim arbitration read 40 stale pre-enqueue CLAIM files (now <= 1, which is reduce_ticket's own newest-CLAIM probe).\n\nAlso added test_all_events_corrupt_reads_as_absent, pinning the terminal case of the newest-first walk (every matching file unparseable -> the type reduces as absent) — the gap the plan review raised as a dropped advisory.","timestamp":1786501422002651001}],"created_at":1786312582640037001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"200fee8d-4cf4-4787-b0aa-6a3dea16dfaf","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"475e-9b99-9085-4b2d"}],"description":"## Context\n\nDesigned under 475e-9b99-9085-4b2d (see its design comment for the full argument and Limits).\n\n`llm/overlap/queue.py::_events_of` opens and `json.load`s EVERY matching event file, and\n`reduce_ticket` calls it three times per ticket. `enrich_drain.maybe_drain` calls\n`pending_enrichment` as its \"cheap gate\" on every write against a 20 ms budget\n(`overlap_drain_gate_budget_ms`). Measured on this repo's live tracker (3,727 ticket dirs):\nthe gate does 11,181 `listdir` calls and 4,977 file opens per invocation, and logs\n`enrich drain gate check took 404.9 ms (> 20 ms budget)` on every rebar command (observed\n404-654 ms). The opens term grows without bound as enrichment re-runs accumulate; the budget\ndoes not.\n\n`digest_sidecar.latest_ticket_digest` is already bounded (sorts dirents, walks newest-first,\nreturns on the first parseable payload) and needs no change. This ticket is the queue side only.\n\n## Plan\n\nMake the queue reduce read newest-first and lazily, changing no on-disk behaviour.\n\nThe event filename is `{timestamp}-{uuid}-{TYPE}.json` where the prefix is the same monotonic\ntimestamp the reducer compares (`_store/event_append.py::event_filename`, built by\n`_prepare_event` from the validated event's own timestamp). Timestamps are fixed-width ns\nintegers, so lexicographic filename order is timestamp order. Therefore:\n\n- `_latest(dir, TYPE)` reads only the LAST matching dirent, falling back to the next-older on a\n  parse failure - the same shape `latest_ticket_digest` already uses. 1 open per type per ticket.\n- `claim()` arbitration needs only CLAIM events newer than the latest ENQUEUE, which are a\n  contiguous suffix of the sorted names; walk newest-first and stop once a filename's timestamp\n  prefix is `<=` the enqueue timestamp. Bounded by the contention window, not history.\n\nThis deletes nothing, renames nothing and writes nothing, so `docs/concurrency.md` invariant I1\nand cross-clone union merges are untouched.\n\nAlso pin the implicit coupling the optimisation depends on: a test asserting that the filename\ntimestamp prefix equals the event body's `timestamp` field for an appended event. Without it a\nfuture writer that names files differently would silently mis-reduce.\n\nScope note: this fixes the ASYMPTOTE (the opens term), not today's constant - `listdir`\ndominates at current scale, so the gate will still breach 20 ms. Do not claim the budget breach\nis resolved; that needs a separate lever (a store-level index, or a cheaper drain gate).\n\n## Testing\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py tests/unit/test_ticket_digest_store.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -q` (the two-clone union-merge regression from be8a0c0595 must stay green)\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `reduce_ticket` opens at most one file per event type per ticket in the no-corruption case, proven by a test that counts `open` calls against a ticket dir seeded with many ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE events.\n- [ ] `claim()` arbitration reads only CLAIM events newer than the latest ENQUEUE, proven by a test that seeds pre-enqueue CLAIM events and asserts they are not opened.\n- [ ] A corrupt newest event file falls back to the next-older one, proven by a test that writes invalid JSON as the newest file and asserts the reduce still resolves.\n- [ ] A test asserts the appended event's filename timestamp prefix equals its body `timestamp` field, pinning the ordering assumption the suffix read depends on.\n- [ ] Existing claim/drain semantics are unchanged: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] No event file is deleted or renamed by this change, verified by the diff touching no `os.unlink`/`os.remove`/`os.rename` call.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py","reason":"Replace the all-files _events_of reduce with a newest-first suffix read in _latest and claim() arbitration"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","reason":"Pin the per-type open count, the pre-enqueue CLAIM skip, and the corrupt-newest fallback"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store.py","reason":"Pin that the event filename timestamp prefix equals the event body timestamp field, the ordering assumption the suffix read depends on"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c0953950-a4f6-49d4-918f-558418c5578c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["enrichment","performance"],"ticket_id":"ea2a-1571-efdc-4447","ticket_type":"task","title":"Bound the enrichment queue reduce read: newest-first suffix scan in overlap/queue.py","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["650bbd59-5c7d-4a20-81b7-33cdea397e2c","200fee8d-4cf4-4787-b0aa-6a3dea16dfaf","015f8810-0b69-4fe5-a5aa-3bb2cc8a9138","98964ec6-fe64-4dee-952b-0926385c4409","0dbf3908-6b97-40a6-b282-bf1505ad6f31","c0953950-a4f6-49d4-918f-558418c5578c","8f48466a-1eb6-4861-a79b-551300c66b8f","7a7ae71e-96a2-4eff-8d5c-dd88c5b817aa"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786501422002651002,"uuid":"d78b7717-c5d2-4549-a995-cd7baba08614"}